Package: MaxMin
Title: Maximum-Minimum Diversity and Dispersion Subset Selection
Version: 0.0.0.9002
Authors@R:
    person("Martin R.", "Smith",
           email = "martin.smith@durham.ac.uk",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-5660-1727"))
Description: Selects a maximally dispersed subset of a fixed set of candidate
    items under the Max-Min Diversity Problem (MMDP, the discrete p-dispersion
    objective): maximise the minimum pairwise distance within the chosen
    subset. Provides a tiered toolbox that operates on a distance matrix, on
    Euclidean coordinates without materialising the distance matrix, or on an
    on-demand distance-column oracle for spaces with no coordinate embedding:
    deterministic Gonzalez farthest-first selection (Gonzalez 1985)
    <doi:10.1016/0304-3975(85)90224-5> with a choice of peripheral seeding
    strategies and a robust ensemble default, the DropAdd tabu-search heuristic
    (Porumbel, Hao & Glover 2011) <doi:10.1007/s10479-011-0898-z>, an exact
    node-packing integer program (Sayyady & Fathi 2016)
    <doi:10.1016/j.ejor.2016.02.026>, a GRASP with path-relinking heuristic
    (Resende, Marti, Gallego & Duarte 2010)
    <doi:10.1016/j.cor.2008.05.011>, and a local-search polish.
